## Recommendation

Use **`status === 'pending'`** as "new pedido needing attention" — it's the only status the codebase already treats this way (dashboard's realtime + polling fallback both key off `pending` specifically to trigger sound/title-flash alerts; `confirmed` is explicitly the "already acknowledged, awaiting kitchen" state). Build a new backend endpoint mirroring the motoboy pattern exactly — e.g. `GET /api/restaurante/pedidos/count?status=pending` (or `restaurante/delivery/pending/count`) using the same `.select('id', { count: 'exact', head: true }).eq('restaurant_id', ...).eq('status', 'pending')` shape as `contarSolicitacoesPendentes`, filtered additionally to `canal !== 'presencial'` (matching the delivery page's own filter at `restaurante-delivery/index.jsx:131`) so dine-in orders don't inflate the Delivery badge — rather than reusing `getCaixa()`, since that's a much heavier payload not designed for global-header polling every 30s.
